WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.000
Imagine this - it’s summer vacation and you're a&nbsp;
kid. You and your friends are playing in the woods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.960
near your neighborhood, just like you've been&nbsp;
doing most days during the break from school.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.640
One day, you spot a treehouse. It’s not that&nbsp;
high off the ground and it's very simply built&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.200
from leaves, grass, and scraps of wood.
You and your friends are curious, so you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:27.040
decide to check it out. Upon investigation, you&nbsp;
find a kid in there. He says his name is Billy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:31.920
and this is his treehouse. You don't recognize&nbsp;
him from school, but you figure he must just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:37.280
be new in town. He asks if he can join your&nbsp;
group, and, wanting to be nice to the new kid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:42.960
you tell him “okay.” You spend the rest of the&nbsp;
day playing with him - games like hide and seek,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.680
tag, and red rover, until it's time&nbsp;
for everyone to go home for dinner.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.880
Strangely, Billy doesn't seem to&nbsp;
leave, he just stays in his treehouse.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.120
For the rest of the week, playing with Billy&nbsp;
and his treehouse become a regular fixture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.560
of your daily routine, but oddly enough, he&nbsp;
never comes to hang out at any of your houses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.440
and you never seem to see him anywhere&nbsp;
else but in the woods. One day, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:12.960
he decides to invite one of your friends, Amy,&nbsp;
to hang out with him at the treehouse alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.440
You think nothing of it, but after&nbsp;
that point, you never see Billy again.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:22.480
It’s a couple of weeks before you and your friends&nbsp;
see Amy again, and when you do, she appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:28.320
off somehow. She seems to be spending a lot of&nbsp;
time in that treehouse. Billy has disappeared,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.800
but you and Amy and the rest of the kids keep&nbsp;
meeting up to play together in the woods.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:38.960
One day Amy pulls you aside, she wants you to come&nbsp;
meet with her tomorrow at the treehouse… alone.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:46.080
This is typically how an SCP-974 infestation&nbsp;
begins - with a mysterious new kid inviting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.680
a group of friends to hang out in his crudely&nbsp;
made treehouse. But as you might have guessed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.680 --> 00:02:01.280
this kid isn't a kid - he's SCP-974, a carnivorous&nbsp;
monster that only looks like a human child. It can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:07.840
live on small woodland animals, but its preferred&nbsp;
prey… is kids between the ages of 6 and 12,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:12.480
taking the phrase 'you are what&nbsp;
you eat' to the next level.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:16.800
The entity will install itself in an&nbsp;
area with a sufficient amount of trees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:22.000
in proximity to a decent population of children.&nbsp;
It will then construct a crude treehouse to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:28.240
serve as its nest, and begin befriending groups&nbsp;
of between 2 and 5 children. The creature will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:33.760
engage in normal outdoor games and allow its new&nbsp;
'friends' to come and go as they please, building&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:39.920
the trust of its newfound playmates. But then,&nbsp;
after about a week, it will select its victim.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:45.760
SCP-974 will single out one member of the&nbsp;
group and invite them to the treehouse alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.720
Whether they accept or deny the invitation&nbsp;
is irrelevant, because this is the point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:57.440
where SCP-974 will strike, subduing and&nbsp;
then devouring that child. After doing so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:03.440
the creature will disappear from the area, going&nbsp;
into a state of hibernation for roughly 12 days.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:08.080
During that time, it goes through a period&nbsp;
of metamorphosis, transforming from whoever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:13.120
it looked like before into an exact&nbsp;
likeness of the child it just consumed.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.600
SCP-974 will continue this cycle&nbsp;
of selecting and catching prey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:20.880
until there are no children&nbsp;
left in the surrounding area.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:27.920
While it's initially friendly to children, SCP-974&nbsp;
has an intense fear of any older human beings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:32.148
The mere presence of a person older than 13&nbsp;
is enough to trigger the creature's fight or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.148 --> 00:03:37.840
flight response, and it will run away if it sees&nbsp;
any adults coming. When running isn't an option,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:46.720
SCP-974 will resort to violence to defend itself.&nbsp;
Despite its looks, SCP-974 is much stronger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.280
faster, and more resistant to damage&nbsp;
than a child, and it has been known to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:56.080
completely rip adults apart in situations&nbsp;
where it felt threatened and cornered.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:04:01.120
SCP-974 does not appear to be affected&nbsp;
by bullets or striking weapons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:06.800
and the only reliable way to put down an instance&nbsp;
seems to be with fire. When infestations are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:12.320
discovered in the wild, the normal SCP foundation&nbsp;
protocol is to attempt to capture the creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:16.800
but if deadly force is required, agents&nbsp;
will set fire to the creature's nest and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.640
a portion of the surrounding area&nbsp;
until it has been confirmed dead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:24.640
before covering up the destruction as&nbsp;
the result of a regular forest fire.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:31.360
The SCP foundation was able to capture one&nbsp;
instance of SCP-974 and place it in containment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:36.000
hoping that having one in captivity would&nbsp;
provide insight into the creature's origins.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.880
It was placed in a lightly wooded&nbsp;
enclosure at Zoological Reserve Site 16,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:45.920
where it immediately started constructing multiple&nbsp;
treehouse nests from the plant life it found.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:51.760
Initially, the containment of SCP-974 involved&nbsp;
offering the creature live human prey.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:55.680
Once every 3 months, a group of&nbsp;
4 children would be brought in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:01.280
in accordance with Protocol 12. The children&nbsp;
would be given room and board in on-site barracks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:08.560
and encouraged to explore the enclosure and play&nbsp;
with SCP-974. If 974 had not selected a victim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:14.480
within 5 days, the group of children would be&nbsp;
sent away and a new group would be introduced.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:19.360
This system worked for a few years, but as&nbsp;
you might expect, the Ethics Committee had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:23.680
a problem with the practice of offering&nbsp;
up live children to a deadly anomaly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:29.840
Now, as of January 1st, 2015, the team at&nbsp;
Zoological Reserve Site 16 are no longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:37.440
able to evoke Protocol 12 in order to acquire&nbsp;
children. Attempts to use another SCP - SCP-1680,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:44.080
a collection of clones of a missing 8-year-old&nbsp;
boy - failed, as SCP-974 refused to eat them.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:47.120
The procedures then changed&nbsp;
to only allow small animals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:49.600
to be introduced into the enclosure as prey.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:56.160
While it might seem like this was a good idea that&nbsp;
would stop SCP-974 from killing any more children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:00.560
like a lot of seemingly good changes to&nbsp;
containment procedures in the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:04.880
this well intentioned move would&nbsp;
ultimately have deadly consequences.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:10.560
SCP-974 at first seemed to behave normally&nbsp;
despite being denied its favorite food.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:16.320
But then, on August 16th, 2015, while&nbsp;
on their weekly sweep of the enclosure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:20.400
patrol teams found that 974 had&nbsp;
destroyed all of the treehouses it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:26.160
had built in its time in containment. The&nbsp;
SCP itself was also nowhere to be found.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:31.600
There was something new in the enclosure&nbsp;
though, a small oval of disturbed soil. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:36.240
geological team was called in, and through&nbsp;
ground penetrating radar, it was found that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:42.400
there was a humanoid figure buried there, curled&nbsp;
up in a fetal position. This couldn't be SCP-974,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:47.440
could it? The figure was much too long and&nbsp;
thin to be anything resembling a human child.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:53.360
But it had to be SCP-974 - it was the only&nbsp;
living thing in the enclosure. The scientists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:58.240
were intrigued, and they theorized that the&nbsp;
SCP might have been entering a new life stage.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:03.680
Further scans were conducted over the next 10&nbsp;
days. During that time, the creature never moved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:08.320
from its position, though it did continue&nbsp;
to grow. It seemed like it was absorbing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:13.280
nutrients from the surrounding soil. The team&nbsp;
decided to exhume the creature to examine it.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:20.640
When they dug it up, they found that SCP-974 had&nbsp;
stretched out, now measuring 220 cm in length and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:27.760
weighing just 37.4 kilograms. It had no features&nbsp;
or orifices of any kind anywhere on its body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:33.520
and its now pale white skin was covered in&nbsp;
some kind of sticky mucus that, when examined,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:40.160
was found to contain a previously undiscovered&nbsp;
enzyme. The creature was alive, but barely. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:46.560
wasn't breathing, and its heartbeat was extremely&nbsp;
slow, almost to the point of being undetectable.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:54.240
SCP-974 was examined for an additional four weeks,&nbsp;
after which it died, and was sent for dissection.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:58.560
Some of the scientists and researchers at&nbsp;
Zoological Site 16 were disappointed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:02.960
hear about 974's death. As vicious&nbsp;
and feral as the creature was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:08.160
they'd developed a certain fondness for it,&nbsp;
and its many little treehouses. Luckily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:12.640
it wouldn't be too much longer&nbsp;
until a new specimen was obtained.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:20.560
On October 16th, 2016, a group of no less than&nbsp;
7 instances of SCP-974 were discovered near a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.960
major American city. The containment team&nbsp;
was forced to kill 6 of the anomalies in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:31.120
the attempts to capture them, but one instance&nbsp;
survived and was taken to Zoological Site 16.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:36.240
As was mandated, the area was burned and&nbsp;
Foundation counterintelligence disseminated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:41.040
a cover story about a forest fire caused&nbsp;
by an improperly extinguished campfire.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:48.160
The new SCP-974 was, like the original one, placed&nbsp;
in the enclosure and denied human prey. Also like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:53.840
the first one, this 974 buried itself after being&nbsp;
denied its preferred meals for several months.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:59.040
The decision was made to leave the SCP&nbsp;
underground longer than in the first instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:03.600
to see what it might become if this&nbsp;
developmental stage wasn't interrupted.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:10.960
On January 25th, 2017, the creature finally&nbsp;
dug itself free from the earth. Now designated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:19.360
SCP-974-A, it was far more aggressive than any&nbsp;
instance of 974 had ever been before. As soon as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:23.760
it was free from the dirt, it made a beeline&nbsp;
straight for the nearest monitoring station.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:28.560
It ripped the roof off and tore the 6 team&nbsp;
members stationed there to shreds in just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:33.840
90 seconds. When the response team&nbsp;
arrived 15 minutes later, only 12%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:40.160
of the human remains were able to be recovered.
But, strangely enough, it at first seemed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:45.920
one of the team had been spared. Georgia Stone,&nbsp;
one of the monitoring team, was severely injured,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:50.880
but apparently in a stable condition.&nbsp;
Disoriented, she approached the response team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:55.120
begging for assistance and urging them to&nbsp;
take her out of the enclosure. But the team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.120 --> 00:10:01.200
was skeptical - they knew that SCP-974 could&nbsp;
become an exact copy of any child it consumed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:07.280
so it followed that the fully-grown&nbsp;
SCP-974-A might be able to copy adults.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:13.040
They asked Georgia questions in order to confirm&nbsp;
her identity, but she was unable to answer them.

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:18.880
Having been found out, SCP-974, still&nbsp;
mimicking Georgia, attacked the response team.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:24.080
They'd been armed with flamethrowers, but&nbsp;
unfortunately, on top of its resistance to damage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:28.880
the adult form of 974 didn't seem&nbsp;
to be afraid of, or harmed by,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:35.040
fire. The team was at a loss for how to kill this&nbsp;
thing, or even subdue it long enough to get out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:41.840
safely. SCP-974-A was tearing through the&nbsp;
members of the team like they were made of paper.

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:46.080
Thinking quickly, one member of the&nbsp;
response team, a guard named Emilio,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:52.160
pulled out one of his standard issue Foundation&nbsp;
hand grenades. When SCP-974-A came at him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:57.280
he pulled the pin and, holding the grenade,&nbsp;
shoved his arm into the creature's open mouth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:04.240
While the explosion destroyed Emilio's arm,&nbsp;
it didn't even break the skin of SCP-974-A.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:10.320
However, it did result in serious damage to&nbsp;
its internal organs, which finally killed it.

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:14.480
Following its death, an autopsy was&nbsp;
conducted, revealing enough about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:19.760
creature that a new file of effective methods&nbsp;
of extermination was able to be created.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:25.520
After this event, the protocols for SCP-974&nbsp;
containment were completely overhauled.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:31.680
Any instances of SCP-974-A seen in the wild&nbsp;
are to be killed as quickly as possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:36.560
More disturbingly though, the ethics committee&nbsp;
rescinded their previous decision, and any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:42.560
instances of 974 that are brought into containment&nbsp;
are to be provided with human prey again.

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:48.560
Letting SCP-974 kill children might not be&nbsp;
a very humane way of keeping it contained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:54.400
but given how much more aggressive and hard to&nbsp;
kill this SCP's adult form is, any option that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:59.920
stops the creature's metamorphosis from happening&nbsp;
is likely the best option in the long run.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:05.120
So remember: If ever you’re out in the woods&nbsp;
and see a crudely constructed treehouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:12.640
perhaps think twice about how innocent it is.&nbsp;
There could be something hungry lurking inside…

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:17.440
Now go check out our playlist with the&nbsp;
entire tale of “SCP - 5000 - The Suit”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:22.640
for an epic saga about a Foundation gone&nbsp;
bad, and one man’s quest to find the truth!

